 "symbols": {
  "RNAV": "rover navigation frame: x forward, y right, z down; origin and orientation set by the deck survey",
  "camera frame": "x right, y down, z along the optical axis (COLMAP)",
  "az, el": "RSM azimuth and elevation (rad) from the product label (resolver values unless angles says encoder)",
  "T, T0": "Navcam camera (plate) temperature of the frame and the reference -20 C",
  "Rz(a), Ry(a)": "right-handed rotation matrices by angle a about z and y",
  "Rot(v)": "rotation matrix of the rotation vector v (axis * angle)",
  "W": "rover side of the azimuth stage: rotation from RNAV into the azimuth-zero frame (contains the 180 deg convention flip, the azimuth zero offset and the azimuth-axis tilt)",
  "P": "the azimuth axis point where the axis meets the RNAV plane z = 0 (P_x, P_y), m",
  "G": "rotation applied to the position model: azimuth-axis tilt (x, y) and azimuth zero (z) as seen by the camera centres; independent of W",
  "h": "offset of the elevation axis from P, in the azimuth-rotated frame (x along the boom, z vertical = elevation-axis height), m; h_y is 0 by convention (folded into c_y)",
  "c_L, c_R": "camera centre of NL / NR from the elevation axis, in the head (elevation-rotated) frame, m; c_y is the lateral position of the eye from the azimuth axis (h_y folded in)",
  "y_L, y_R": "lateral position of NL / NR from the azimuth axis (h_y + c_y), m; y_L - y_R is the stereo baseline",
  "Q_L, Q_R": "rotation from the head frame to the NL / NR camera frame (the camera pointing in the head)",
  "k_az, k_el": "scale on the resolver angles: angle used = angle (1 + k)",
  "qT_L, qT_R": "camera-frame pointing rate per eye (rad/C), applied as Rot(qT (T - T0)); x/y parts are principal-point motion (dcx = fx qT_y, dcy = -fy qT_x), z is roll"
 },
